BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Hamilton Lugar School
DTSTART:20261026T160000Z
DTEND:20261026T170000Z
LOCATION:Zoom
SUMMARY:Center for Refugee Studies Op-Ed Initiative Webinar Series
DESCRIPTION:The CRS Op-Ed Initiative\, open to faculty\, students\, and t
 he CRS community\, teaches participants how to convert research insights 
 into accessible\, public-facing op-eds. This four-course series covers ho
 w to develop\, write\, edit\, and publish op-eds\, and why opinion writin
 g is an important vessel for spreading innovative ideas and sparking impo
 rtant discussions. Participants do not need any prior publication experie
 nce to join\, and the course is free.The series is led by Assistant Direc
 tor Meredith Perkins\, who has six years of experience writing over 50 op
 -eds as a freelance journalist in student\, local\, and national publicat
 ions. She won the 2024 and 2025 Region 4 Society of Professional Journali
 sts Best College Opinion Writing award and the 2023 Ohio News Media Assoc
 iation Best Collegiate Column Writing award. A current Master of Public A
 ffairs-Master of International Affairs student\, her past newsroom experi
 ence inspires her to make complex academic conversations accessible for p
 ublic audiences.Session 1: Before You Writewill introduce the history and
  purpose of op-eds and the range of places where opinion writing appears\
 , including local and national newspapers\, industry publications\, depar
 tmental blogs\, and platforms such as Substack. We will review genre conv
 entions of op-eds\, why op-eds are useful\, and what information writers 
 should know (e.g. workplace media policies) before considering publicatio
 n.Session 2: Drafting Your First Op-Edwill focus on identifying a strong 
 and timely argument. Participants will examine who is already writing abo
 ut their topic\, the dominant conversation surrounding it\, and recent ne
 ws or research that might create an opportunity for commentary. A central
  exercise will help participants identify the "knowledge gap" between wha
 t they know through expertise\, research\, or lived experience and what a
  general reader is likely to know. Participants will use that gap to deve
 lop a clear\, relevant argument for a public audience.Session 3: Editing 
 Your Op-Edwill help participants turn a draft into an accessible\, public
 ation-ready piece. Topics will include common word-count requirements\, c
 lear and concise language\, reducing jargon\, checking hyperlinks and sou
 rces\, anticipating possible misunderstandings\, proper image attribution
 \, headline writing\, and basic search engine optimization. After the ses
 sion\, participants can send drafts to the instructor for personalized fe
 edback.Session 4: Publishing and Pitching Your Op-Edwill help participant
 s identify the right outlet for their work based on the audience they hop
 e to reach. The session will compare features and challenges of publishin
 g in local and national newspapers\, industry publications\, institutiona
 l blogs\, and independent platforms. Participants will learn what to incl
 ude in a submission or pitch\, such as a brief description\, author bio\,
  word count\, contact information\, and headshot\, as well as how to reco
 gnize potential red flags. The session will conclude with an editor's per
 spective on what happens behind the inbox\, including high submission vol
 ume\, response times\, competition for limited space\, and why many submi
 ssions may be read without receiving a reply.By the end of the series\, p
 articipants should understand how to identify a compelling op-ed idea\, c
 ommunicate specialized knowledge to a general audience\, edit a piece to 
 common publication standards\, and develop a realistic strategy for publi
 cation. Participants who work on a piece throughout the program may leave
  with a completed or near-completed op-ed and a list of appropriate outle
 ts to approach.    &#160\;  Register to attend at https://go.iu.edu/cVZV1
 S (https://go.iu.edu/cVZV1S) to get the Zoom link.
