 led the office responsible for U.S. engagement in APEC\, and served a
 s former U.S. Secretary of State Mike Pompeo's director of the offi
 ce of Chinese and Mongolian Affairs. She was posted overseas in Beijing
 \, Islamabad\, Jerusalem\, and Quito. Her previous domestic assig
 nments include office director for economic policy in the Bureau of E
 ast Asian and Pacific Affairs\, special assistant to then-Secretary of St
 ate Condoleezza Rice\, and Lebanon desk officer.   Ms. Beran speaks M
 andarin and Spanish. She joined the Foreign Service in 2002 and g
 raduated from Claremont McKenna College in 1999.
