SUMMARY:Ostrom Workshop | Research Series: Camilo Rey-Sabogal
DESCRIPTION:&#160\;Bio  Dr. Camilo Rey-Sabogal is an Associate Professor 
 at the Faculty of Social Sciences and Education\, Universidad de Cartagen
 a\, Colombia. He investigates the political economy of urban space\, focu
 sing on how territorial transformations shape access to housing\, work\, 
 and rights for vulnerable populations. His research examines residential 
 segregation\, migration\, gentrification\, housing policy and urban inequ
 alities\, with sustained fieldwork in Cartagena and the Colombian Caribbe
 an.Title  Land Scarcity and Flood-Risk Zoning: How Tourism Gentrification
  and Climate Change Limit Affordable Housing in CartagenaAbstract  Over t
 he past two decades\, Cartagena has undergone major housing market transf
 ormations driven by tourism-driven real estate speculation\, the financia
 lization of housing\, climate-driven flooding risks\, and migration press
 ures. This research examines how tourism gentrification and the reduction
  of buildable land due to flood risk jointly constrain affordable housing
  production in Cartagena\, and identifies institutional arrangements capa
 ble of improving the governance of scarce\, secure urban land under condi
 tions of real estate pressure and climate vulnerability.  The study emplo
 ys a mixed-methods approach combining quantitative spatial analysis of ho
 using price dynamics across urban submarkets\, multi-layered vulnerabilit
 y mapping\, and institutional analysis of planning mechanisms. It address
 es three core questions: (1) How do tourism-driven gentrification dynamic
 s generate ripple effects across housing submarkets that reduce the avail
 ability and affordability of social housing? (2) How do climate-related f
 lood risks exacerbate land scarcity and affect vulnerable households' acc
 ess to housing? (3) What institutional arrangements and governance mechan
 isms could reduce the social housing deficit in contexts shaped by real e
 state pressure and climate risk?About the Ostrom Workshop Research Series
   Learn about innovative research by Graduate Students and Visiting Schol
 ars as they advance the mission of the Ostrom Workshop\, building upon th
 e theme of governance to understand and address major societal problems.
