SUMMARY:Great Faculty Debate: Constantino vs Macekura
DESCRIPTION:Zachary Constantino\, Professor of Practice in International 
 Studies\, spent twenty years in the U.S. government working on security\,
  diplomacy\, and intelligence\, including roles at the Defense Intelligen
 ce Agency\, the State Department\, and the Office of the Secretary of Def
 ense. Stephen Macekura\, Professor of International Studies\, is a histor
 ian of U.S. foreign relations\, development\, and political economy\, and
  the author of The Mismeasure of Progress.  Expect sharp questions\, civi
 l debate\, and plenty of time for audience Q&amp\;A.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p dir="ltr">  Zachary Constantino\, Profess
 or of Practice in International Studies\, spent twenty years in the U.S. 
 government working on security\, diplomacy\, and intelligence\, including
  roles at the Defense Intelligence Agency\, the State Department\, and th
 e Office of the Secretary of Defense. Stephen Macekura\, Professor of Int
 ernational Studies\, is a historian of U.S. foreign relations\, developme
 nt\, and political economy\, and the author of <em>The Mismeasure of Prog
 ress</em>.</p><p dir="ltr">  Expect sharp questions\, civil debate\, and 
 plenty of time for audience Q&amp\;A.</p>
