SUMMARY:2026 Graduate Career Diversity Symposium\, "Maximize Your PhD"
DESCRIPTION:Graduate Career Diversity Symposium 2026: Maximize Your PhDCa
 reers Beyond Academia  Are you looking ahead to your professional traject
 ory after your graduate program? Whether you are completely set on indust
 ry or just starting to explore options outside or alongside the tenure tr
 ack\, this upcoming event is designed specifically for graduate and PhD s
 tudents ready to translate their advanced training into high-impact caree
 rs.Why You Should AttendHear from Successful Alumni: Listen to TED-style 
 talks and Q&amp\;A sessions from PhD alumni now thriving in industry role
 s. Learn how they made the leap\, navigated the job market\, and leverage
 d their graduate skills.  Get Direct Insights from Employers: Industry pr
 ofessionals will break down core professional competencies and how to eff
 ectively translate academic research into industry value.  Explore Specia
 lized Career Pathways: Join concurrent afternoon sessions tailored to you
 r goals\, including a dedicated networking and strategy session for inter
 national graduate students.  Build Your Toolkit: Participate in hands-on 
 walkthroughs of career platforms like Beyond Graduate School and Beyond t
 he Professoriate.  Connect Over Lunch: Enjoy a networking lunch in the Fr
 angipani Room to connect with peers\, alumni\, and industry professionals
 .  Key Agenda Highlights9:15 AM – 10:15 AM: Welcome Breakfast &amp\; Op
 ening Remarks (Frangipani Room)  10:15 AM – 11:00 AM:Connecting Your Fu
 ture: Alumni Insights on Careers Beyond Academia. Featuring alumni speake
 rs sharing career discovery and skill-building journeys.  11:10 AM – 12
 :00 PM:Inside Industry Research: What Employers Want &amp\; How Grad Skil
 ls Translate12:00 PM – 1:00 PM: Networking Lunch  1:15 PM – 2:45 PM: 
 Concurrent Afternoon Sessions. Hands-on career mapping\, alumni Q&amp\;A\
 , employer perspectives\, and networking.  2:45 PM – 3:00 PM: Closing R
 emarks &amp\; Feedback  Don't miss this opportunity to bridge your disser
 tation research with your future professional career!
