 un their own executive advisory firms.</p><h4 data-path-to-node="17">  Va
 lue for Every Degree Level</h4><ul data-path-to-node="18"><li><p data-pat
 h-to-node="18\,0\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="18\,0\,0" data-index-in-n
 ode="0">Undergraduate Students:</strong> Learn how to break into competit
 ive sectors like foreign policy\, national security\, and tech strategy d
 irectly from women who held those roles.    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-
 node="18\,1\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="18\,1\,0" data-index-in-node="
 0">Master Students:</strong> Get realistic strategies for translating gov
 ernment and public policy tradecraft into high value roles in corporate p
