 rong> Managing teams and making critical decisions when information is li
 mited and stakes are high.    </p></li></ul><h3 data-path-to-node="22">  
 Speaker Profiles</h3><p data-path-to-node="23"><strong data-path-to-node=
 "23" data-index-in-node="0">Belinda Jackson Farrier</strong></p><p data-p
 ath-to-node="24">  Belinda Jackson Farrier is the Founder of Sweetgrass A
 dvisory Group and co-host of the <i data-path-to-node="24" data-index-in-
 node="87">Leadership Tea Podcast</i>. She served as a career member of th
 e Senior Foreign Service with the U.S. Department of State\, holding post
 ings in Rwanda\, El Salvador\, Togo\, and Peru. In Washington\, her assig
 nments included the State Department Operations Center\, the White House 
 Situation Room\, and the Washington Foreign Press Center. She later joine
 d Google\, where she served as Director for Global Rapid Response in YouT
 ube Trust and Safety.</p><p data-path-to-node="25"><strong data-path-to-n
 ode="25" data-index-in-node="0">Shelby Smith-Wilson</strong></p><p data-p
 ath-to-node="26">  Shelby Smith-Wilson is the Founder of The FendAll Coll
 aborative and co-host of the <i data-path-to-node="26" data-index-in-node
 ="83">Leadership Tea Podcast</i>. A senior government executive\, diploma
 t\, and leadership strategist\, her global career spans five countries. S
 he specializes in change and crisis management\, strategic negotiation\, 
 and cross-cultural leadership\, advising senior executives on guiding org
 anizations through complex structural transitions and high stakes disrupt
 ions.</p>
